0..76 Comment "// A category with families as a theory whose sorts depend on earlier sorts."
77..154 Comment "// Contexts and substitutions form a category, a type lives in a context, and"
155..229 Comment "// a term has a type in a context (Huang and Angiuli, _Fat cell structures"
230..302 Comment "// and generalized algebraic theories_, doi:10.4230/LIPIcs.LICS.2026.58,"
303..314 Comment "// § 1.1)."
315..317 Comment "//"
318..388 Comment "// Dependent type theory states its syntax and its models through this"
389..461 Comment "// signature. `Tm(g, a)` reads `a` at the sort `Ty(g)`, so a term\'s sort"
462..538 Comment "// names the context of its type. Comprehension extends a context by a type,"
539..616 Comment "// and substitution moves types and terms between contexts. The block\'s value"
617..685 Comment "// of `Theory` keeps each index as data, so a program reads it back."
686..688 Comment "//"
689..762 Comment "// The standard model reads a context as a type. A type in a context is a"
763..838 Comment "// family over it, and a term is a section of that family. The block states"
839..913 Comment "// the category laws and the laws on types. Their rules carry each context"
914..985 Comment "// that a substitution stands between, so two identities compose at one"
986..1054 Comment "// context and the unit laws join. The twin keeps the laws on terms."
1055..1057 Comment "//"
1058..1072 Comment "// - see: #522"
1073..1088 Comment "// - see: #5016"
1089..1104 Comment "// - see: #5017"
1105..1120 Comment "// - see: #5042"
